Bundled fonts — IBM Plex
================================================================================

TerMinal uses the IBM Plex typefaces:

  - Desktop: via the @fontsource/ibm-plex-sans and @fontsource/ibm-plex-mono
      npm packages (a dependency, not vendored source).
  - iOS: the .ttf files vendored at ios/TerMinalRemote/Fonts/ (IBM Plex Sans
      Regular/Medium/SemiBold, IBM Plex Mono Regular/Medium).

IBM Plex is Copyright (c) IBM Corp., licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
Version 1.1 <https://openfontlicense.org>. The OFL is a separate licence from
TerMinal's MIT: the fonts may be bundled and redistributed under its terms, and
those terms are NOT superseded by LICENSE. Reserved Font Name: "IBM Plex".

================================================================================
vendor/agentview — third-party reference submodule
================================================================================

vendor/agentview is a git submodule pointing at an UNRELATED third-party
project (https://github.com/the-real-adammork/agentview), kept purely as a
reference. It is:

  - NOT built, bundled, imported, or shipped in any TerMinal artifact,
  - optional to fetch — a plain `git clone` without --recurse-submodules leaves
    it empty and everything still builds,
  - licensed by its own upstream, on its own terms; TerMinal's MIT LICENSE does
    not cover it and makes no claim over it.

CI's machine-path check and the repo's own tooling exclude vendor/ for the same
reason: it is not our code.
